  "goodToKnow": "Strafen means to punish, but in modern German it's mostly found in set phrases: jemanden mit Verachtung strafen, Wer zu spät kommt, den bestraft das Leben (life punishes those who come too late, attributed to Gorbachev in 1989). The everyday verb is bestrafen. Die Strafe is punishment or a fine: eine Strafe zahlen. Strafbar means punishable, and das Strafgesetzbuch (StGB) is the criminal code."
